  "notes": "This is CMS's own 'how to read your EOB' teaching example, not a real member's EOB -- identity fields (patient name, claim number, provider, payer) are deliberately printed as literal 'XXXXXX' placeholder text, not real values; a correct extraction returns null for these, not the placeholder string itself. The document has 2 real service line rows plus a 'Total' row with real dollar figures -- ClaimFlow's EOB schema is scalar (no line_items list), so this gold uses the document's own printed 'Total' row for provider_charges/allowed_charges/plan_paid/patient_responsibility/deductible/coinsurance/copay, which is the only single-record-shaped real data on the page. denial_or_remark_codes is schema-typed as list[str] but only one code (PDC) appears on this document. is_bill=False is the one field this document is entirely about -- 'THIS IS NOT A BILL' is printed in large bold text at the top."
